<li about="#cite_note-513" id="cite_note-513" data-mw-footnote-number="391"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwNXk"><a href="#cite_ref-513" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwNXo"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwNXs">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-513" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><abbr class="abbr indicateur-format format-pdf" title="Document au format Portable Document Format (PDF)" about="#mwt2074" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwNXw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"pdf","href":"./Modèle:Pdf"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'>[PDF]</abbr> <span class="ouvrage" about="#mwt2075" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwNX0" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lien archive","href":"./Modèle:Lien_archive"},"params":{"langue":{"wt":"en"},"url":{"wt":"http://www.ukmediacentre.pwc.com/imagelibrary/downloadMedia.asp?MediaDetailsID=863"},"titre":{"wt":"UK Economic Outlook"},"horodatage archive":{"wt":"20070610175146"}},"i":0}}]}'><abbr class="abbr indicateur-langue" title="Langue : anglais" id="mwNX4">(en)</abbr> <span class="noarchive" id="mwNX8">«<span typeof="mw:DisplaySpace" id="mwNYA"> </span><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20070610175146/http://www.ukmediacentre.pwc.com/imagelibrary/downloadMedia.asp?MediaDetailsID=863" class="external text" id="mwNYE">UK Economic Outlook</a><span typeof="mw:DisplaySpace" id="mwNYI"> </span>»</span> <small id="mwNYM">(version du <time class="nowrap" datetime="2007-06-10" data-sort-value="2007-06-10" id="mwNYQ">10 juin 2007</time> sur <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Internet_Archive" title="Internet Archive" id="mwNYU">archive.org</a>)</small></span>, chiffres de 2005 (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/PriceWaterhouseCoopers" title="PriceWaterhouseCoopers" class="mw-redirect" id="mwNYY">PriceWaterhouseCoopers</a>)<span typeof="mw:DisplaySpace" id="mwNYc"> </span>; d'après cette étude, Tokyo, New York et Los Angeles distancent Chicago, Paris et Londres qui ont des PIB comparables<span typeof="mw:DisplaySpace" id="mwNYg"> </span>; toutefois, Londres dépasserait Chicago et Paris d'ici à 2020.</span></li>
